    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Yordan Alvarez** stands out as the clear anchor of the Zurich Zebras lineup with a dominant 87.42 efficiency score. While we are awaiting official confirmation on his spot in the batting order, the combination of his elite 0.449 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Melton makes him a must-start, providing the highest ceiling for RHR production. The most aggressive play, however, is **Pete Crow-Armstrong** at 76.65. Despite facing a tough arm in Peralta, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is maximized by his leadoff position and a distinct stolen base advantage against a pitcher with a slow delivery, providing the speed equity we prioritize to chase the scarcest category in our 5x5 build. **Junior Caminero** also earns a strong recommendation at 72.81, as he successfully navigates a neutral park and decent platoon leverage to remain a high-floor cornerstone for our infield.\n\nManaging our roster depth requires constant recalibration; **Pedro Ramirez** was the hardest omission, finishing just outside the cut at 43.04. While he provides useful versatility, his lower projected efficiency compared to the high-upside speed profiles of **Caleb Durbin** and **Luke Raley** kept him on the bench, as we continue to prioritize volume of production in the middle infield. We are keeping a close eye on **Lars Nootbaar**, who presents a solid 62.94 score, but his start comes with a 42% rain risk that could lead to an abbreviated outing. Meanwhile, **Casey Schmitt** remains a marginal play at 50.03, though he receives a slight boost from wind conditions; he stays in the lineup to preserve our game caps while maintaining a steady presence against Springs. We will continue to monitor the status of **Dillon Dingler** and **Kyle Schwarber** to ensure they capitalize on their respective spots in the order against Cavalli and Imai.",
